    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0490" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/3244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Roumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vopicka</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-28">December 28,
                            1918</date>.<lb/>[Received January 2, 1919—5:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. The committees of Transylvanians which brought the documents for the union of
                    Transylvania with Roumania<anchor n="24" xml:id="d338-f1"/> came to the <pb
                        facs="0491" n="403" xml:id="pg403"/> Legation and asked me to extend their
                    hearty thanks to President Wilson and our country for freeing them from the
                    Hungarian yoke.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vopicka</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
